<section class="container" style="padding-block:4rem 2rem;max-width:760px;">
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">In the liberalised energy market, municipal utilities no longer compete only with the neighbouring supplier but with nationwide providers that win customers on price alone. In that comparison, a single undifferentiated tariff makes a utility interchangeable — however good its actual service.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Stadtwerke Bielefeld therefore did not need a new advertising message but an understandable structure: a family of tariffs that clearly distinguishes different customer needs (price sensitivity, preference for green electricity, planning certainty) without overwhelming customers with complexity.</p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 3rem;max-width:900px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Structure as the real service</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The task here lay less in design as such than in order: a clear, consistent brand architecture for several tariff products that can be told apart at a glance yet recognisably come from the same system.</p>
  <div class="case-img reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
    <img src="/img/Stadtwerke-Markenfamilie.jpg" alt="Stadtwerke Bielefeld — overview of the tariff brand family">
  </div>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-2">Transparency became the real point of difference against nationwide low-cost providers.</p>
</section>

